-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]

Currently, OpenWrt can be installed on the R6080 only by using the [[https://github.com/jclehner/nmrpflash|nmrpflash]] tool. Follow the documentation there to install nmrpflash and use it to flash the OpenWrt image. Please note that while the nmrpflash page says that some devices can be flashed by nmrpflash wirelessly, the R6080 requires a direct Ethernet connection to the workstation running nmrpflash.

After the final power-cycle in the flashing process, the device should be accessible over SSH, on the LAN ports, with no password. LuCI is still not running.

  $ ssh root@192.168.1.1

The overlay file-system may not be available so it may not be possible to save configuration changes. To initialize it:

  root@OpenWrt:~# jffs2reset
  root@OpenWrt:~# reboot

Connect to R6080 over SSH again:

  $ ssh root@192.168.1.1

To install LuCI:

  root@OpenWrt:~# opkg update
  root@OpenWrt:~# opkg install luci

At this point LuCI should be accessible at http://192.168.1.1/
==== Flash Layout ====

^ Layer0 |  raw flash, 8192 KiB  |||||||
^ Layer1 |  **mtd0** \\ ''u-boot'' \\ 256 KiB  |  **mtd1** \\ ''factory'' \\ 128 KiB  |  **mtd2** \\ ''nvram'' \\ 192 KiB  |  **mtd3** \\ ''firmware'' \\ 7552 KiB  |||  **mtd7**  \\ ''reserved'' \\ 64 KiB  |
^ Layer2 |:::|:::|:::|  **mtd4** \\ ''kernel'' \\ 1920 KiB  |  **mtd5** \\ ''rootfs'' \\ 5632 KiB  ||:::|
^ Layer3 |:::|:::|:::|:::                       |  **''/dev/root''** \\ 2560 KiB  |  **mtd6** \\ ''rootfs_data'' \\ 3072 KiB  |:::|



